  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 122 AM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nThe ever-present mid-level high pressure system slides off to the \neast this weekend. At the same time, a mid-level open wave on the \nsouthern periphery of this high will slowly graze the central Gulf \ncoast as it moves onshore. This increased relative vorticity maxima \nwill enhance the seabreeze more so for locations east of the upper \nTexas coast. Aside from the morning rain chances along the Coastal \nBend this morning and then the afternoon seabreeze convection \nfurther inland, the seabreeze won't be as active as it has been the \nlast few days as our upper-level disturbances move away. \n\nGiven the lack of much upper-level pattern change, temperatures this \nweek look very similar each day with minimal rain chances. Moderate \nto Major HeatRisk will be in play each afternoon, with the Brush \nCountry seeing peaks of Extreme HeatRisk, though not enough to \nwarrant any heat-related headlines at the moment.",
